% 42 U.S.C. 1382c(a)(1) — us:statutes/42/1382c/a/1
the text of "42 USC 1382c(a)(1)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382c/a/1.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382c(a)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382c/a/1.yaml".

the aged age threshold years is 65, as stated in "42 USC 1382c(a)(1)(A)".

rule aged_blind_or_disabled_individual with provenance "42 USC 1382c(a)(1)":
a person is aged blind or disabled individual if
    the individual age years of the person is a number N
    and the aged age threshold years is a number M
    and N >= M
    or the person is blind as determined under paragraph 2
    or the person is disabled as determined under paragraph 3
    and the person is resident of united states
        and the person is citizen of united states
            or the person is alien lawfully admitted for permanent residence
            or the person is alien otherwise permanently residing in united states under color of law
            or the person is alien lawfully present due to section 1182 d 5 application
        or the person is child citizen of united states
            and the person is living with parent member of armed forces assigned to permanent duty ashore outside united states.


