rule couple_or_living_with_spouse_resource_limit with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(A)":
the couple or living with spouse resource limit of a person is an amount if
    the person is a person
    and the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B i and paragraph 2 B is the amount.

rule individual_no_spouse_resource_limit with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(3)(B)":
the individual no spouse resource limit of a person is an amount if
    the person is a person
    and the resource limit amount for paragraph 1 B ii is the amount.


% 42 U.S.C. 1382f(a) — us:statutes/42/1382f/a
the text of "42 USC 1382f(a)(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382f/a.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382f/a.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)-(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382f/a.yaml".

the annual rounding multiple is 12, as stated in "42 USC 1382f(a)(2)".

rule prior_rounding_carryover_increase with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)":
the prior rounding carryover increase of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the unrounded dollar amount that would have been in effect for month but for prior rounding of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

rule amount_after_paragraph_1_increase with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)":
the amount after paragraph 1 increase of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the prior rounding carryover increase of the statutory dollar amount is an amount K
    and N = M + K.

rule subsection_a_applicable_increase_percentage with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(2)":
the subsection_a applicable increase percentage of a statutory dollar amount is a rate R if
    the subchapter ii increase of the statutory dollar amount was determined on wage increase percentage
    and the subchapter ii benefit increase percentage for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number N
    and the cpi basis subchapter ii increase percentage for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the maximum of N and M is R
    otherwise the subchapter ii benefit increase percentage for month of the statutory dollar amount is R.

rule amount_after_subsection_a_increase with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(2)":
the amount after subsection_a increase of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the amount after paragraph 1 increase of the statutory dollar amount is an amount M
    and the subsection_a applicable increase percentage of the statutory dollar amount is a rate R
    and the annual rounding multiple is an amount K
    and N = floor(M * (1 + R) / K) * K.

rule prior_rounding_carryover_increase_for_section_1382_b_1_amount with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)":
the prior rounding carryover increase for section 1382 b 1 amount of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the unrounded section 1382 b 1 dollar amount that would have been in effect for month but for prior rounding of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the section 1382 b 1 dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

rule amount_determined_under_section_1382f_for_section_1382_b_1 with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)-(2)":
the amount determined under section 1382 f for section 1382 b 1 of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the section 1382 b 1 dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the prior rounding carryover increase for section 1382 b 1 amount of the statutory dollar amount is an amount K
    and the subsection_a applicable increase percentage of the statutory dollar amount is a rate R
    and the annual rounding multiple is an amount P
    and N = floor((M + K) * (1 + R) / P) * P.

rule prior_rounding_carryover_increase_for_section_1382_b_2_amount with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)":
the prior rounding carryover increase for section 1382 b 2 amount of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the unrounded section 1382 b 2 dollar amount that would have been in effect for month but for prior rounding of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the section 1382 b 2 dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

rule amount_determined_under_section_1382f_for_section_1382_b_2 with provenance "42 USC 1382f(a)(1)-(2)":
the amount determined under section 1382 f for section 1382 b 2 of a statutory dollar amount is an amount N if
    the section 1382 b 2 dollar amount in effect for month of the statutory dollar amount is a number M
    and the prior rounding carryover increase for section 1382 b 2 amount of the statutory dollar amount is an amount K
    and the subsection_a applicable increase percentage of the statutory dollar amount is a rate R
    and the annual rounding multiple is an amount P
    and N = floor((M + K) * (1 + R) / P) * P.


% 42 U.S.C. 1382(a)(1) — us:statutes/42/1382/a/1
the text of "42 USC 1382(a)(1)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/1.yaml".

the text of "42 USC 1382(a)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/42/1382/a/1.yaml".

the individual annual income base limit is 1752, as stated in "42 USC 1382(a)(1)(A)".

rule applicable_individual_annual_income_limit with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(1)(A)":
the applicable individual annual income limit of a person is an amount N if
    the individual annual income base limit is an amount M
    and the amount after subsection_a increase of the person is an amount K
    and the maximum of M and K is N.

rule eligible_individual_1 with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(1)":
a person is eligible individual if
    the person is aged blind or disabled individual
    and it is not the case that the individual of the person has eligible spouse
    and the annual income other than excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount N
    and the applicable individual annual income limit of the person is an amount M
    and N <= M
    and the individual of the person has spouse with whom living
    and the resources other than excluded pursuant to section 1382 b_a of the person is an amount K
    and the couple or living with spouse resource limit of the person is an amount P
    and K <= P.

rule eligible_individual_2 with provenance "42 USC 1382(a)(1)":
a person is eligible individual if
    the person is aged blind or disabled individual
    and it is not the case that the individual of the person has eligible spouse
    and the annual income other than excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount N
    and the applicable individual annual income limit of the person is an amount M
    and N <= M
    and it is not the case that the individual of the person has spouse with whom living
    and the resources other than excluded pursuant to section 1382 b_a of the person is an amount K
    and the individual no spouse resource limit of the person is an amount P
    and K <= P.

